Package: dash-phonecon
Version: __VERSION__
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-pyside6.qtcore, python3-pyside6.qtgui, python3-pyside6.qtwidgets, python3-websockets
Recommends: python3-dbus, pulseaudio-utils, bluez, libspa-0.2-bluetooth
Maintainer: Dash PhoneCon Project <dash-phonecon@localhost>
Homepage: https://github.com/shrijayan/dash-phonecon
Description: Answer and control Android phone calls from Ubuntu
 Dash Phone Con shows a popup when your Android phone rings, with the
 caller's name and number, and lets you answer, decline, or hang up
 without touching your phone - a system tray icon shows connection and
 call status at a glance.
 .
 It also makes a best-effort attempt to route call audio through this
 computer's speakers and microphone over Bluetooth Hands-Free once a call
 is active (the packages under Recommends enable this; the core features
 above work over WiFi alone even without them).
 .
 Requires the companion Android app (see the project's android/
 directory) installed on your phone and pointed at this computer's IP
 address - both must be running for this to work.
